<ContentPage
  title="Affiliate Disclosure | SpedCentral"
  description="SpedCentral's disclosure of affiliate relationships and how they affect product recommendations, in line with FTC guidelines."
  heading="Affiliate Disclosure"
  lastUpdated="July 27, 2026"
>
  <p>
    In line with the FTC's guidelines on endorsements and affiliate marketing, here's exactly how SpedCentral makes
    money from the products we list.
  </p>

  <h2>What this means</h2>
  <p>
    Some links to products on SpedCentral are <strong>affiliate links</strong>. If you click one and make a
    purchase, we may earn a small commission from the retailer or brand -- at no extra cost to you. The price you
    pay is the same whether or not you came from SpedCentral.
  </p>

  <h2>What this doesn't mean</h2>
  <p>
    An affiliate relationship never determines which products we choose to feature or how we describe them. We
    also work with independent creators who sell digital downloads (like printable visual schedules) directly
    through SpedCentral; we take a percentage of that sale, which is separate from affiliate commissions but works
    the same way in principle -- clearly priced, no hidden markup to you.
  </p>

  <h2>Sponsored vs. affiliate</h2>
  <p>
    "Sponsored" (used on provider and some product listings) means someone paid for featured placement. "Affiliate
    link" means we earn a commission if you buy after clicking. A listing can be one, both, or neither -- we don't
    combine the two into a single vague label, because they mean different things.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href="mailto:hello@spedcentral.com">hello@spedcentral.com</a> if you have questions about how a
    specific listing is monetized.
  </p>
</ContentPage>
